WEBVTT

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.020
What is it?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.110
Oh, nothing!

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:17.240
"Friday, June 10th"

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.410
"Friday, June 10th"

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.410
Rika, no matter how many times
you check the calendar,

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:24.910
until you change your mind
and accept Hinamizawa in your heart...

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:30.840
...you will never escape June of 1983.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.050
"Higurashi: When They Cry SOTSU"

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.450
I'm heading out, Dad.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.120
Stay safe... oof.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.750
Are you okay? Want me to bring you
some water, or some medicine?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.080
No, I'm fine.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.340
I just had a bit too much
to drink last night in Okinomiya.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.920
Were you drinking with Rina-san again?

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.760
Yeah, she's really great.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.640
You know, if you want,
I'd love for you to meet her, Reina.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.310
Oh, look at the time!

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.560
I'm gonna be late meeting up
with my friends. See you later!

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.060
S-Sure.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:07.530
"Hinamizawa"

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.500
Keiichi-kun! Good morning!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.750
Why are you always here so early?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.000
You can sleep in
every now and then, you know.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:26.640
Hey, there they are.
You guys sure took your sweet time!

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.100
Says the girl who always
takes her sweet time.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.270
Morning, Mii-chan!

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.770
Morning, Rena.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:41.360
This is quite the elaborate trap
you're setting today!

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.150
My, whatever do you mean?

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:49.490
Creating multiple webs to ensnare
your hapless enemy...

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:53.160
...is the utmost essence of trap-setting!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.380
Clap, clap, clap!
You're so good at this, Satoko!

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.880
Here he comes!

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.550
Trying to test my skills, are you?

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.470
"Today's Helper: Satoko Hojo"

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.470
What's going on, guys?

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.590
"Today's Helper: Satoko Hojo"

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.590
Stay back, Rena! She's here!

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.430
"Today's Helper: Satoko Hojo"

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.430
Huh? By she, you mean...

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.520
Could this be any more obvious,
Satoko Hojo?!

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.660
Poor, poor Keiichi!
He's starting his day off rough!

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.580
Satoko!

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.830
"Sunday, June 12th"

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.170
Thanks for hanging out
with me, Keiichi-kun.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.170
Did you have fun today?

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:44.300
Yeah, loads! I'm kinda bummed
we're all going home.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:49.220
Okay, well... would it be okay if we stopped
somewhere on our way back? Would it?

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.350
Sure, but where?

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:53.350
"NO TRESPASSING"

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:58.100
Wonder what's here, wonder what's here!

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:05.780
You wanted to go climb
a pile of trash, Rena?

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:09.620
It's not trash! To me, it's a pile of treasure!

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.160
Maybe I'll find something kyute...
I can't wait, I can't wait!

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.080
Hey, hold up!

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.210
It's okay, you just wait over there, Keiichi-kun!

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:23.590
Sheesh.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:38.350
Something kyute, something kyute...

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.740
I knew it! A Kenta-kun!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.990
But he's stuck... how do I get him out?

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.830
Keiichi-kun!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.250
Sorry to keep you waiting! I'm all done!

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.250
Tomitake-san?

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.350
That Kenta-kun was so kyute!

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.850
What's wrong, Keiichi-kun?

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:26.530
Huh? O-Oh, just sad we couldn't
bring him home for you.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.650
Yeah.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.570
If I'd been there, I would've...

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:34.160
...grabbed 'im by the arm
and yanked him outta there!

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.790
No way! You would've ripped
Kenta-kun's arm off!

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:46.840
Y-Yeah, we wouldn't want that.
Want him to have all his arms.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:52.890
I-It's fine! I promised, remember?
I'm gonna help you get him home.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:58.310
Thank you! I get to
take him home <i>with </i>you!

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.940
See you later.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.100
Yup! See you tomorrow!

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.450
I'm back.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.160
Hey. Welcome back, Reina.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.200
You're heading out
right now, Dad? It's so late.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:23.120
Yeah, she called and said
she wanted to see me, so...

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.580
I'll try not to be out too late.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.170
Her again?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.550
Huh? Did you say something?

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.260
Nope! It's dark out, so be careful.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.430
Right. I'll be careful, don't worry.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.560
I'll be back, Reina.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.940
Have fun, Dad.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:54.280
I can't be so down in the dumps.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:56.740
The whole reason I dropped
the "i" from my name

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.910
was so I could forget all
the <i>icky </i>things that happened.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.600
"Gentlemen's Club"
"NO. 23
Rina"

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.110
"Monday, June 13th"

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:43.200
You'll never beat me in a race, Rika!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.670
But we're not racing!
We're on a scavenger hunt!

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:49.250
I can still win this!

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:55.840
Guess there'll be no hard feelings
about whoever wins, then!

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.010
I'll give it everything I've got!

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:10.150
Knowing Mii-chan, she probably put it
somewhere Keiichi-kun would never find it!

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.240
"STORAGE"

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.460
--Rena!
--Keiichi-kun!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:35.960
Rika!

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:40.260
I knew you'd be here, Satoko.
Great minds think alike!

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:46.230
Oh, dear. That makes this
a race now, doesn't it?

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:49.350
You've got no time for "nipah"s now!

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:56.690
--Pardon me!
--I'm taking the lead!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.160
I don't think so!

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.840
Sounds like <i>someone </i>just won!

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:20.220
You're still no match for
my ingenious traps, sweet, little Rika!

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.100
Satoko, I think that's enough...

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:29.390
It's okay, I lost. I'm not mad about it at all.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.730
In fact, I've got a present
for you for winning, Satoko!

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.940
Oh, Rika, I knew you,
of all people, would understand!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.820
Congratulations, Satoko!

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.250
Wh-What on Earth just happened?!

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.250
Satoko, look at your face...

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.170
What in the world?!

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:02.590
I brought it to fight back
against your traps, Satoko!

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:06.430
Looks like you're no match for Rika-chan.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:09.520
Rena?

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:14.440
Oh, sorry, maybe I'm just tired
from all this fun! I'm a little exhausted.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:15.980
You okay?

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:19.780
Yeah. I think I'm gonna go rest
in the nurse's office then go home.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:22.400
--Poor Kenta-kun...
--Don't worry!

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.990
Once you're feeling better,
I'll come help out!

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.630
I'm going to go wash my face.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:40.420
There's no way I can go out
in public like this!

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:46.680
Guess that's it for today.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.080
Please forgive me, Rena-san.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:20.750
This is all Rika's fault,
that ignorant fool.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:31.970
I promise to create a Hinamizawa
where you're happy.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:36.730
Where you'll smile and laugh every day.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.310
So forgive me, Rena-san,

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:42.530
and everyone else
who's about to experience this.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.700
I'm so terribly sorry.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.180
Satoko-chan?

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.970
Is someone in here?

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.730
I've gotta get home.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.020
I'm home.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:15.120
"I had to run to Okinomiya--
something suddenly came up.
--Dad"

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.640
Our savings...

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:41.060
This is the settlement money
Mom gave Dad in the divorce.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:43.060
We're not supposed to touch it
unless it's an emergency!

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:45.440
Why?!

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.080
Reina-chan,

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:02.580
do you remember the man
who came with us to dinner?

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.840
Yeah, Uncle Akihito?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:09.380
Oh, I have to stop calling him Uncle,
or he's gonna hit me!

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.930
Reina-chan, do you like Akihito-san?

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:17.890
I hate him! He always teases me.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:21.730
Well, that's because he likes you.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.230
You got along well
at the barbeque, though!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:28.650
Sometimes he's okay. Sometimes.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:35.410
Reina-chan, who do you like better--
me, or your father?

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:40.160
You, because you let me
eat these yummy parfaits!

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:45.210
If I went to live in a different house
than your father...

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:51.340
...who would you want to live with?

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:53.130
Uh... Huh?

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:57.220
I'm thinking...

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:01.640
...about divorcing your father
and getting married to Akihito-san.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:06.440
Why?! You don't like Dad anymore?!

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:14.110
Poor Dad! He didn't do anything wrong!

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:19.950
He did <i>everything </i>for you
so you could focus on work!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:23.660
And now you're going to leave him?!
I hate you!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.120
I'm sorry, it's too late.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:31.130
Why?! You haven't told Dad yet, right?!
It's not too late!

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:35.930
It is.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.510
I'm pregnant.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:39.850
Huh...?

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.560
"Divorce Settlement Agreement"
"Reiko Ryugu"

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.270
"Divorce Settlement Agreement"
"Reiko Ryugu"

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.270
And that's that.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:48.770
Remember--now, not only are you
not allowed to meet your ex-wife,

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:50.570
you also cannot contact her
for any reason.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:55.110
You agreed upon these terms,
so do not violate them.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.420
Reina?

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.960
Do you know the man she left me for?

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.260
Yeah.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.600
He's a funny man who gives me candy.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:37.910
I'm sorry! I-I'm so sorry, Reina!

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:41.620
Up until that moment, I believed...

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:45.790
...that I had to be nice to <i>everyone</i>,
no matter what.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.330
But then I learned something.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:53.750
There are some bad people in the
world who don't deserve kindness.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:57.720
I shouldn't have been nice to him.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.470
Uncle Akihito was a bad person.

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:06.980
I should've shunned him.
Because he was a bad person!

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:10.230
If I'd shunned him,
our family wouldn't have broken apart!

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.150
But it did, because I didn't
work hard enough!

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:19.490
And now it's falling apart again.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:26.580
I have to work hard,
or my family will fall apart again.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.410
I have to do something.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:31.630
I have to do <i>something</i>.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:41.430
"Flower Road"

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:53.270
Hey there, buddy! Wanna take a load off?
We got real cuties inside!

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.190
We'll be here all night!

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:58.490
Whoa, hold on there, sweetheart!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:00.360
--Can I--
--No, no, no!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.490
Come back when
you're older, mmkay?

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.750
Can I get a black tea?

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.890
What am I doing out here?

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:37.690
You sure you should be leaving
your favorite customer

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:39.190
all alone back there, Rina?

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:44.410
C'mon, he's blacked-out drunk.
I don't wanna wake him up.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:47.450
I ordered a bunch of expensive drinks,

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:51.290
so he'll wake up, pay for them,
and head back to Hinamizawa.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:55.290
You're getting him to pay for booze
you're not even gonna drink?

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.590
God, what a sucker.

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:59.380
Mm-hmm.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:04.010
Apparently, he's got boatloads of cash
from when his wife divorced him,

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:06.260
and he'll jump to pay for anything I want.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:09.520
He sure is earning you a pretty penny.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:14.520
I bet if you told him, "I gotta pay
off my ex..." he'd fork it all over!

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.270
Probably.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.280
Seriously, talk about a sucker!

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:26.030
Ohmigosh, do you know any guys
who'd wanna help out?

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:33.910
Sheesh, you look pretty depressed
for a girl with her own personal ATM.

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:38.290
Well, he's got a teenage daughter.

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:40.710
So what?

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:44.420
I was raised by a single parent too, so...
I kinda sympathize.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.720
Maybe it's time to break things off.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.470
What? What happened to
the Rina I thought I knew?

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:54.230
Nothing. Just if he gets any more serious,
it's gonna be a pain for me.

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:58.060
I have to work harder.

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:03.030
I have to work even harder.

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:05.740
I have to work harder.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.820
I have to work harder.

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:50.090
"<i>Oniakashi-hen</i>:
Demon-Revealing Chapter, Part 2
Next time: "<i>Oniakashi-hen</i>:
Demon-Revealing Chapter, Part 2."
